  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Formulating inequalities for a dietary supplement program</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A county health facility in Turkana designs a dietary supplement program for expectant mothers using blends of local nutrient-rich grains. Let \( x \) represent the amount of finger millet (in grams) and \( y \) represent the amount of amaranth grain seeds (in grams) in a single serving.</p>
<ul>
<li>The combined single-serving daily portion weight must not exceed <b>{@W@} grams</b>.</li>
<li>Each gram of finger millet provides <b>{@A@} mg</b> of iron, and each gram of amaranth provides <b>{@B@} mg</b> of iron.</li>
<li>The combined mixture must deliver a minimum daily therapeutic target of at least <b>{@N@} mg</b> of iron.</li>
</ul>

<p><b>a) </b> Write the linear inequalities that model these two physical and nutritional limitations. <i>(Use \( \le \) or \( \ge \) as appropriate. Do not include the non-negativity constraints \(x \ge 0, y \ge 0\) in your answers below.)</i></p>

<p>Daily portion weight constraint: [[input:ans1]]</p>
<p>Therapeutic nutrient constraint: [[input:ans2]]</p>

<div><b>Weight check:</b> [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div><b>Nutrient check:</b> [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> Due to a supply shortage, the facility must prepare a serving containing <b>zero grams</b> of finger millet.</p>
<p>Based on your therapeutic nutrient constraint, what is the absolute minimum weight of amaranth grain seeds (\(y\)) required to meet the daily iron target?</p>
<p>Minimum amaranth required: [[input:ans3]] grams</p>

<div><b>Calculation check:</b> [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: Formulating the Constraints</b></p>
<p>1. <b>Daily Portion Weight Constraint:</b> The total physical mass of the food blend is capped at \({@W@}\) grams. "Must not exceed" translates to less than or equal to (\( \le \)):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{{@ta1@}} \)</p>

<p>2. <b>Therapeutic Nutrient Constraint:</b> The total iron contribution from both components must satisfy the dietary threshold of \({@N@}\) mg. "At least" translates to greater than or equal to (\( \ge \)):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{{@ta2@}} \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Evaluating a Boundary Condition</b></p>
<p>We are given that \( x = 0 \). We substitute this value directly into our therapeutic nutrient inequality to find the minimum required amount of amaranth (\(y\)):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
{@A@}x + {@B@}y &amp;\ge {@N@} \\
{@A@}(0) + {@B@}y &amp;\ge {@N@} \\
{@B@}y &amp;\ge {@N@} \\
y &amp;\ge \frac{{@N@}}{{@B@}} \\
y &amp;\ge {@ta3@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>
<p>Therefore, if no finger millet is used, the daily serving must contain an absolute minimum of <b>{@ta3@} grams</b> of amaranth grains to fulfill the safety threshold.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
